@page rh="HOUSE AUREM · BELL · THE RECORD AND THE MAN" m="TKC: DR3 · TL; VOL. I · {v1:temple} · {v1:sorted}"
# The record and the man
plate: doc
dh: Binding Certificate | TEMPLE OF AURELIA
dsub: SIGNED BENEATH EACH HUSBAND'S NAME
df: Officiating | Senior Minister Bell
df: Bride | ____________
df: Husband | ____________
df: Witness | a Vowed officiant
stamp: BOUND
/end
rec:
His office | Signs Binding certificates beneath each husband's name and sponsors Assessment candidates (DR3).
Celeste | Thirty-four years. Her sweet potato pie at harvest suppers, and a call every winter when the Temple needs coats repaired. He greets her with both hands and calls her Mother Parish. She answers "Morning" and he keeps smiling (DR3).
Eden | He kept her waiting while he signed certificates. He asked whether her father was dead and whether her mother was properly Bound when she was born, not about her grades. He offered Leah Home Instruction and prayed every door shut that wasn't intended for her (DR3).
The Assessment | He speaks before the scores about "divine order, talent as stewardship, and elevation as burden," reads Proverbs 31.29 from the Book of Covenant, and closes, "May every daughter receive with grace the portion appointed to her" (DR3).
prompt: Why he wouldn't sponsor her, in his own words, to his wife that night | fill

@page rh="HOUSE AUREM · BELL · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE" m="1 SAM 1.12–16; 1 SAM 2.12–17; AMOS 7.10–13; REV 3.7–8; PROV 31.29; VOL. I · {v1:hannah} · {v1:b-twelve} · {v1:teaches}"
# Faith and scripture
rec:
What he believes | "The House always judges fairly" (DR3). INFERENCE: He believes in the Temple's order sincerely, and it's never cost him anything.
What he preaches | Divine order, talent as stewardship, elevation as burden (DR3).
His name | *Bell* has no biblical source. INTERPRETATION: A bell calls people in and tells them what time it is.
Eli · 1 Samuel 1–2 | POSSIBLE: The priest at Shiloh who watches a praying woman's lips move and decides she's drunk. His sons abuse the office, and he rebukes them and does nothing (1 Sam 2.12–17, 22–25). **Where it breaks:** Eli corrects himself when Hannah answers him. Bell never asked Eden a question he didn't already have an answer for.
Amaziah · Amos 7 | POSSIBLE: The priest of Bethel who tells a prophet to go home, because "it is the king's chapel, and it is the king's court" (7.13). **Where it breaks:** Amos answers him to his face. Eden went home and found the clause.
tab:
| He quotes | Never preached from his pulpit |
| Proverbs 31.29, "Many daughters have done virtuously, but thou excellest them all" (DR3) | Revelation 3.8, "I have set before thee an open door, and no man can shut it" |
| _ | Amos 7.14–15, a herdsman God sent anyway |
small: Volume One: Hannah and Eli's misreading, {v1:hannah}. The Twelve, with Amos, {v1:b-twelve}. What the Temple teaches, {v1:teaches}.
prompt: The prayer, word for word, as he said it over Eden | fill

